# claude-anfs settings: shipped by stack/claude, read by its settings writer
# (~/.local/lib/claude/anfs/settings), which puts anfs's coordinator hooks into ~/.claude/settings.json.
#
# This machine's values go in ~/.config/claude-anfs/claude-anfs.local.env, beside this file (yours,
# never shipped). The environment wins over both. Format: NAME=value, one per line, read and never
# sourced. A commented line is the default used when nothing sets it. `~/.local/lib/claude/anfs/settings
# config list` shows them and where each is from; `... settings config set NAME=value` writes the
# local file and rewrites ~/.claude/settings.json at once.

# The Claude Code status line in ~/.claude/settings.json: `space: <space> role: coordinator|none`
# in a space, nothing elsewhere. Written only when the file has no statusLine of yours; off leaves
# it out and takes ours out
#CLAUDE_ANFS_STATUSLINE=on
